UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Eight of Swords represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Paralysis"—the high-anxiety phase where the sovereign consciousness, having engaged in evasive maneuvers (the Seven), finds itself trapped within a self-constructed cage of its own, projected fears. Moving beyond the strategic stealth of the Seven, the Eight signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Imprisonment," where you are objectively free to move, but your cognitive protocols have been so severely hijacked by limiting belief-loops that you are experiencing total, functional immobilization. Visually depicted as a blindfolded figure surrounded by eight upright swords, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Cognitive Dissonance"—the realization that the "bars" of your cage are not external constraints, but the rigid, low-frequency data-points of your own, past-based assumptions. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Processing Lockdown," where you are running massive, high-cost simulation loops of "worst-case scenarios" that are effectively consuming all your available CPU cycles. When the Eight of Swords appears, your system is registering a "Self-Imposed Stasis" status; you feel trapped, and you are being invited to stop the "victim-narrative" of your external circumstances and instead perform a brutal, diagnostic audit of your own, internal logic-gates. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your perception. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional De-blocking": recognizing that the blindfold can be removed, and that the swords do not form a barrier, but are simply markers of the very thoughts you have refused to release. To inhabit the Eight of Swords is to master the art of "Strategic Un-blindfolding," recognizing that by simply acknowledging that your "trapped" state is a byproduct of your own, analytical fear, you are effectively dismantling the cage and reclaiming your full, sovereign freedom of movement.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Eight of Swords appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Awakening," "Constraint-Collapse," or the catastrophic—yet profoundly liberating—realization that the cage you have been living in has never actually been locked. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "fear of freedom" with "safety," even as your internal operating system is experiencing a major, critical failure of its "containment" protocol. You are essentially "stepping out of the illusion," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "stay protected" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually face the responsibility of your own, newly discovered autonomy. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "prisoner," while internally, you are being jolted by a profound, gnawing sense of possibility, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency agitation, the experience of "fearing the light," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your "imprisonment" was a self-maintained performance. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of self-limitation"; you are obsessively trying to find reasons why you "cannot" move, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final exit is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to walk away from the cage, you would be forced to own the consequences of your own, present-day, sovereign life. The reversed Eight of Swords exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "accountability," and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense of the "helpless victim" and step into the open, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these victim-aligned, power-denying scripts, perform a brutal audit of your self-imposed limits, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize the integrity of your freedom over the comfort of your cell. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance suppression, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical liberation—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "the known restriction" over the vulnerability of "the unknown expansion," and realizing that until you are willing to take the blindfold off, see the empty space around you, and walk into your own, unfiltered truth, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom cage you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 36;
